chapter.v:
“He who 


slaughters an, 


ox is like one who kills a man; he who sacrifices a lamb, like one who breaks a dog’s neck; he who presents a grain offering, like one who offers pig’s blood; he who makes a memorial offering of frankincense, like one who blesses an idol. These have chosen their own ways, and their soul delights in their abominations;

“Rejoice with 


Jerusalem, and, 


be glad for her, all you who love her; rejoice with her in joy, all you who mourn over her;
